/**
 * The sign-up source for a visit that arrived without `?ref=` (growth
 * diagnosis, 2026-10-20: 69 of 70 sign-ups had no source). The browser's
 * referrer is read for its host only and turned into one short word:
 * `google`, `chatgpt`, `reddit`, or, for a site not in the table, the site's
 * own name (`example-com`). The path, the query and the address itself are
 * never kept or sent; only the word goes on, like a `?ref=`.
 *
 * The landing site (lexpad_landing `site/assets/site-v7.js`) holds the same
 * table, so a visit through lexpad.app and one straight to the app get the
 * same word. Change both together.
 */

/** Exact hosts (after `www.` / `m.` are dropped) and the word for each. */
